ISO-10303-21;
/* Twi162: Single ADVANCED_FACE on PLANE in CLOSED_SHELL; outer EDGE_LOOP has 6 LINE edges forming a star/bow that visits center point (5,5,0) twice: E0 (0,5,0)→(5,5,0), E1 (5,5,0)→(10,5,0), E2 (10,5,0)→(5,10,0), E3 (5,10,0)→(5,5,0), E4 (5,5,0)→(5,0,0), E5 (5,0,0)→(0,5,0); center vertex (5,5,0) appears as both endpoint of E0/E1 and E3/E4 IS the 3-edge-mutual-intersection defect; FixIntersectingEdges pairwise splits create inconsistent topology without shared-vertex reconciliation IS the mechanism; EDGE_LOOP IS wired into FACE_OUTER_BOUND → ADVANCED_FACE in CLOSED_SHELL — never orphaned */
